ne-type attribute is not dashed.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"dashLength"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The length, in tenths, of the spaces in a dashed line. Ignored if the corresponding line-type attribute is not dashed.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"spaceLength"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"position"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"font"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"color"}],"kind":"parameters"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctaveshift\/init(id:kind:number:size:dashlength:spacelength:position:font:color:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"title":"MXLNumberLevel","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","abstract":[{"text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOctaveShift/init(id:kind:number:size:dashLength:spaceLength:position:font:color:)":{"kind":"symbol","title":"init(id:kind:number:size:dashLength:spaceLength:position:font:color:)","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctaveshift\/init(id:kind:number:size:dashlength:spacelength:position:font:color:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLUpDownStopContinue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL21MXLUpDownStopContinueO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"size","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dashLength","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","text":"MXLTenths","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"spaceLength","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLPosition"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"font","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV","text":"MXLFont","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift\/init(id:kind:number:size:dashLength:spaceLength:position:font:color:)","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"MXLOctaveShift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLUpDownStopContinue":{"abstract":[{"text":"The up-down-stop-continue type is used for octave-shift elements, indicating the direction of the shift from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their true pitched values because of printing difficulty.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLUpDownStopContinue","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLUpDownStopContinue","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLUpDownStopContinue","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlupdownstopcontinue","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLUpDownStopContinue"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLFont","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLFont","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFont","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOctaveShift":{"title":"MXLOctaveShift","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOctaveShift"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctaveshift","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift","abstract":[{"text":"The octave shift type indicates where notes are shifted up or down from their true pitched values because of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"printing difficulty. Thus a treble clef line noted with 8va will be indicated with an octave-shift down from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the pitch data indicated in the notes. A size of 8 indicates one octave; a size of 15 indicates two octaves.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOctaveShift"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"abstract":[{"text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"title":"MXLPosition","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","abstract":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTenths":{"abstract":[{"text":"The tenths type is a number representing tenths of interline staff space (positive or negative). Both integer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and decimal values are allowed, such as 5 for a half space and 2.5 for a quarter space. Interline space is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measured from the middle of a staff line.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLTenths","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltenths","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths"}}}